# WorkforceOS security

- Enforce authorization server-side on every mutation and protected read. UI hiding is not security.
- Clerk authenticates. Local PostgreSQL `users`, `roles`, and `user_roles` authorize. Never use Clerk metadata as the sole permission source.
- Candidate data is Restricted PII. Access requires `candidate_pii.read`. Scout and SkillBridge obey the same rule: strip email/phone/compensation/resume before any model context.
- Never put database credentials, Clerk secret keys, storage secrets, or provider API keys in client bundles.
- Validate all external input with schema validation before writes.
- Record audit events for material business changes. Do not log passwords, tokens, or secrets.
- Disabled local users must be rejected even if a Clerk session exists.
- Do not store founder ownership or cap-table information in this application.
